DATA SOURCES (each bound through the ViewModel as StateFlow from the KMP core, P1/S8)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
useDrivetrainHealth  GET /drivetrain/health [vehicle_id]   -> DrivetrainExtrasRepository.drivetrainHealth(id)  (PRIMARY gate)
useDrives            GET /drives [vehicle_id]               -> DrivetrainExtrasRepository.drives(id)
useDrivingStats      GET /drives/stats [vehicle_id]         -> DrivetrainExtrasRepository.drivingStats(id)
useMotorLatest       GET /motor/latest [vehicle_id]         -> DrivetrainExtrasRepository.motorLatest(id)
useMotorHistory      GET /motor [vehicle_id, limit=200]     -> DrivetrainExtrasRepository.motorHistory(id, 200)
  None of the five Driving/motor reads have a shared store method wired into the Android DataContainer (it wires no
  DrivingStore), so they are all served by the page-local [DrivetrainExtrasRepository]: a CachingRepository<JsonElement>
  over the SAME shared ApiHttpClient + CacheStore + cache-then-network operator the shared repositories use
  (CacheDomain.Drives; ADR-013 freshness + SI-verbatim caching). This is the BatteryExtrasRepository precedent for
  store-less reads, kept entirely within com/teslasync/driving so DataContainer is untouched.
scope/settings : SelectedVehicleStore.selectedId (web useSelectedVehicle) + SettingsStore.settings() (web useUnits). No HTTP in the view.
decode         : JsonElement -> typed models in DrivetrainHealthPageModel.parse*/build* ; the view only resolves i18n + draws.
SI boundary    : drive distance (m), motor/module temperatures (°C) and speed (m/s) convert ONLY at render via prefs
                 (convertDistanceFromSI / convertTempFromSI / convertSpeedFromSI; formatEnergy for regen Wh). The
                 /drives/stats total_distance_km + avg_speed_kmh values are fed through the SAME shared converters the web
                 hooks feed them through (byte-identical figure) — the unit-suffixed key names are upstream-owned legacy
                 identifiers (Phase-48), not a second conversion. No miles/°F/psi stored or computed.

