PARITY_COVERED=7

i18n         : every visible literal resolves from res/values/strings.xml via stringResource(R.string.translation_drivetrain_*
               / translation_common_* / translation_error_* / translation_freshness_*); zero hardcoded UI text. Unit symbols
               (kW / Nm / RPM / kΩ / % / °C) and the em dash are web literals, never i18n keys (web parity). 102 page keys
               already existed in the generated catalog; the 8 absent keys (4 sensor labels frontMotor/rearMotor/inverter/
               battery + 4 chart aria labels) existed only as web inline t(key,default) defaults and were added to
               values/strings.xml (MissingTranslation lint is disabled; values-ar/values-he fall back to default).
states       : drivetrain-health is the PRIMARY gate (loading/empty/error/success). A no-vehicle / no-payload response
               routes to the friendly empty surface via DrivetrainHealth.hasData (web `!health`). Each secondary feed
               (drives, stats, motorLatest, motorHistory) renders its own content-or-empty surface so no section is hidden.
a11y/theme   : the four charts carry accessibleDescription (the web aria-labels) + a screen-reader data table; gauges expose
               their own semantics; icons decorative (contentDescription=null); all color via MaterialTheme.colorScheme +
               TeslaTokens.chart (theme-invariant) + TeslaTokens.status (per-theme) — dynamic color + dark theme; typography
               via the role components (PageTitle/SectionTitle/PanelTitle/BodyText/Caption). Compose-native (no webview).
divergences (Honesty #9, documented — not silent):
  - The web `actions` date-range RangePicker is represented by the web's initial default 30-day window (defaultChartWindow);
    the vehicle scope picker (VehicleSelect shared surface) is reproduced. The window is the parity-critical input to the
    per-drive charts; the interactive picker is an actions-slot affordance with no shared Android surface.
  - LiveMotorStatus is ALWAYS rendered (its internal "no live motor telemetry" empty shows when no snapshot) rather than the
    web outer `{motorLatest && …}` conditional — honours the never-hide-sections rule; the empty branch is the web component's
    own EmptyState.
  - The four charts always render their ChartContainer (status=Empty with the no-data message when <2 points) rather than the
    web returning null — honours never-hide-sections and matches the BatteryHealthPage chart precedent.
  - HV Isolation: the web sources isolationResistance from the SSE live state (useVehicleLive); no shared live accessor exists
    on Android yet (grep: zero "isolation" refs in shared-core/android-live), so the metric is reproduced and shows an em dash
    rather than being hidden.
  - Chart horizontal threshold reference lines (normal/warm 60/80°C, warm-zone/freezing) are omitted: the shared Vico
    LineChartWrapper/AreaChartWrapper expose only vertical markers, not horizontal threshold lines. The data series (the
    parity-critical content) render in full.
  - The outside-temperature trend converts each point to the user's unit at the display boundary (consistent with its axis +
    the SI-canonical rule); the web plots the raw Celsius value while converting only the axis/reference lines (a latent web
    inconsistency that only differs under a Fahrenheit preference).

